phase-potentiation	periodization	A muscle built in a high-volume hypertrophy block is not immediately strong — it requires a strength realization block to neurologically wire the new contractile tissue for maximal force output. After 8–12 weeks of accumulation/hypertrophy training (high volume, 60–75% 1RM, RPE 7–8), transition to a strength block: reduce total weekly sets by 40–50%, push load to 80–95% of 1RM, extend rest to 3–5 minutes. Inform the user that the "pump" will diminish — this is expected and correct. The adaptation driver has shifted from metabolic stress to high-threshold motor unit recruitment and rate coding.	[0.015675569,0.009225927,-0.008307899,-0.06578454,0.013466116,-0.011363671,0.010562407,0.011843058,-0.006572929,0.01951105,-0.037636116,0.0027483935,-0.013987265,0.00408964,0.1071512,0.051722456,0.025877764,-0.010407547,0.0005277806,-0.004390603,-0.0070417253,-0.019015312,-0.02056558,-0.010236994,0.0042218002,-0.032481376,0.025779739,0.016721293,0.067930385,-0.013581584,0.004192169,0.0222979,0.0074184053,0.03816628,0.022587229,0.018083224,-0.019438077,-0.042373933,0.025922084,0.011572811,0.029533552,0.024310112,0.036162563,0.01148646,-0.020221448,0.0067824605,0.014546781,-0.018902102,0.009352164,0.02157689,-0.02849133,-0.007405816,-0.021622684,-0.16757396,0.0035453918,-0.0057703517,0.0068606916,0.022849848,0.023476202,-0.0009737487,-0.01970761,0.01649984,0.016734645,-0.00672002,-0.0011867901,-0.023893509,0.039103683,0.0034998758,-0.009560268,0.004319846,-0.019140873,0.00018635114,0.011517245,-0.008492236,-0.00806519,-0.015715297,0.024260752,0.027356414,-0.017150529,-0.018989872,-0.012891238,-0.013796724,0.0098139085,0.012438387,-0.0028255268,-0.016166879,-0.027139107,0.0002894531,-0.0009399278,0.024545971,0.015082927,0.0015469767,0.009519736,-0.001309346,-0.0030328336,-0.008803292,0.024006413,-0.015558567,0.0029276758,-0.0010158203,-0.015271862,0.018946229,-0.00058086833,-0.006108766,-0.037403803,0.011585629,-0.012830254,-0.009982995,0.00511882